## Explanation 

For the RepairCafé ticketing system, I developed a full-stack web application using Next.js, Prisma, and PostgreSQL. The frontend, backend, and database layers are integrated within a single, cohesive codebase. 

An example of this cohesive integration is the process of registering a new item (voorwerp) for repair:

### 1. Frontend Layer (React & Next.js Client Components)
The user interface is built with React client components and styled using Tailwind CSS. In the registration form at [app/counter/register/page.tsx](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/app/counter/register/page.tsx), user input is captured via interactive form fields and submitted directly to a Next.js Server Action:

```tsx
const result = await registerVoorwerp(payload);
```

### 2. Backend Layer (Next.js Server Actions)
The backend logic is implemented as secure Server Actions marked with the `'use server'` directive. In [lib/actions/voorwerpen.ts](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/lib/actions/voorwerpen.ts), the `registerVoorwerp` function performs server-side validations, validates user sessions, handles business logic (such as checking for an active day and generating a unique tracking number), and initiates database operations.

### 3. Database Layer (PostgreSQL & Prisma ORM)
The database schema is defined in [prisma/schema.prisma](https://github.com/Thomas-More-Digital-Innovation/2526-TMEM-001-Ticketing-system-for-repair-cafe/blob/main/code/rc-app/prisma/schema.prisma) with relations between models like `Gebruiker`, `Klant` (Client), `Voorwerp` (Item), and `Cafedag`. The Server Action interacts with the PostgreSQL database using Prisma Client:

```typescript
const created = await prisma.voorwerp.create({
  data: {
    volgnummer,
    klantId: klant.klantId,
    aanmeldingsDatum: now,
    aanmeldingsTijd: now,
    voorwerpStatusId: geregistreerdStatus.voorwerpStatusId,
    afdelingId: afdelingId,
    voorwerpBeschrijving: data.itemDescription,
    klachtBeschrijving: data.problemDescription,
  },
})
```

